# Deploy local → develop

KindNesta uses a **develop-first** Git flow. Production Pages deploys from `main`; day-to-day work goes to `develop`.

## Default branch

- Do all feature work on **`develop`**.
- If the current branch is `main` (or anything else) when making changes, **switch to `develop`** (or create it from `main`) before committing.
- After local changes the user wants saved/shipped: **commit and `git push origin develop`** (not `main`), unless they explicitly ask to update `main` or open a PR.

## Do / don't

```text
✅ git checkout develop
✅ git push -u origin develop
✅ Open PR develop → main when asked to release

❌ git push origin main          (unless user explicitly requests release)
❌ Commit unfinished work on main
❌ Merge to main without the user asking
```

## Release to production

Only when the user asks to release / merge / deploy live:

1. Ensure `develop` is pushed and green.
2. Open or merge PR **`develop` → `main`** (or push `main` only if they explicitly say so).
3. GitHub Actions on `main` publishes GitHub Pages.

## Push notes

- Prefer SSH remote `git@github.com:BarathCommits/KindNesta.git` if HTTPS auth fails.
- Rebuild (`npm run build`) before commit when static `docs/` output must ship with the change.
- Never force-push `main` or `develop` unless the user explicitly requests it.
